      "writtenOn": "2025-12-12T17:00:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right, I forgot about explicit Destroy() calls.\n\nI actually like the TryAddRef() flavour better, since we\u0027re already doing that for UnmapImpl().\n\nAnd I think we could wrap it in another flavour of EnqueueGL() to avoid replicating it everywhere. The idea would be to capture a ref if we can, or a raw pointer if we can\u0027t. Something like this:\n\n```\n    template \u003ctypename Fn, typename T\u003e\n    MaybeError EnqueueGL(T* self, Fn\u0026\u0026 work) {\n        if (self-\u003eTryAddRef()) {\n            return EnqueueGL([self \u003d Ref\u003cT\u003e(self), work](const OpenGLFunctions\u0026 gl) -\u003e MaybeError {\n                return work(self.Get(), gl);\n            });\n        } else {\n            return EnqueueGL([self, work](const OpenGLFunctions\u0026 gl) -\u003e MaybeError {\n                return work(self, gl);\n            });\n        }\n    }\n```\n\nWould that work?",
      "parentUuid": "645194c0_7eef0bf6",
      "revId": "356774029c2d5f0927c9be02044475847c324d18",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
