      "writtenOn": "2025-12-15T11:44:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That would work. However it only works for classes with single handle. It doesn\u0027t work for QuerySet as you mentioned. A `FutureHandle` can work in all cases.\n\nAnd IMHO, the templated DestroyGL + `TryAddRef` approach is quite difficult to read at least for me. Too many indirections, getter function pointer then lambda.\n\nI\u0027m curious what is the issue with the `FutureHandle` container approach? Its main purpose is separating the lifetime of the handle from the Buffer class\u0027. It\u0027s useful for deferrals because after the Buffer object is destroyed, the handle\u0027s destruction is deferred. That `FutureHandle` class\u0027 implementation might even have less code than the templated `DestroyGL` function.\n\n\n\u003e I actually like the TryAddRef() flavour better, since we\u0027re already doing that for UnmapImpl().\n\nActually, after this [CL](https://dawn-review.googlesource.com/c/dawn/+/280016/5/src/dawn/native/opengl/BufferGL.cpp), we can know whether we are being destroyed or not in `UnmapImpl` without `TryAddRef`. So it is no longer needed there.",
      "parentUuid": "d55175e8_a91bc470",
      "revId": "356774029c2d5f0927c9be02044475847c324d18",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
