      "writtenOn": "2025-12-15T17:52:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah thanks for looking into it, I forgot that there were all these special cases, that unfortunate. Both `FutureHandle` and the `EnqueueDestroyGL` have their own problems, and I tried to come up with a few other alternatives but they have their own issues.\n\n - FutureHandle: extra allocations and verbosity.\n - EnqueueDestroyGL: I\u0027m very concerned about `TryAddRef` as that\u0027s used in other load-bearing logic like the destruction of all child objects on device destruction.\n - EnqueueDestroyGL + add an enum to DestroyImpl to say why we are being destroyed. Maybe? But also I didn\u0027t audit the 365 lines that reference it in Dawn.\n - Making all the OpenGL backend objects `WeakRefSupport` and use that somehow: didn\u0027t find a way to make it work.\n - Make the handles `std::optional\u003cGLuint\u003e` to know in `DestroyImpl` if they have been initialized or not: runs into races with the deferred commands running, difficult logic for what to do when initialization only works partially.\n \nLooking at all this, could we move forward with `FutureHandle` and open an issue to investigate adding a `reason` to `DestroyImpl` in the future (but given the amount of code it touches, I don\u0027t think we\u0027ll get to it soon or at all).",
      "parentUuid": "83955743_ed2468eb",
      "revId": "356774029c2d5f0927c9be02044475847c324d18",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
